  "term": "optical defect",
  "definition": "In this historical passage, an optical defect means an apparent problem in vision thought to underlie a visual disturbance. It refers here to seeing numerous dark dots or spots against a white surface, interpreted by the writer as a form of scattered blind areas in the visual field.",
